---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TrustStrip from '../../components/TrustStrip.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CTABand from '../../components/CTABand.astro';
import FAQAccordion from '../../components/FAQAccordion.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I relocate a hardwired charger myself?",
    "answer": "No. Hardwired EVSE units are connected directly to high-voltage 240V circuits. Disconnection and reconnection must be performed by a licensed electrician with proper de-energization and lockout procedures."
  },
  {
    "question": "Will my existing wiring work at the new location?",
    "answer": "If the new location is farther from the panel, wire gauge may need to be increased to prevent voltage drop. If closer, existing conductors can often be reused."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does a relocation require a new permit?",
    "answer": "If the branch circuit is modified, extended, or rerouted, a new electrical permit is required. If the charger is simply remounted on the same wall segment with no circuit changes, a permit may not be needed."
  },
  {
    "question": "How long does a typical relocation take?",
    "answer": "Most relocations are completed in 3 to 6 hours, depending on the distance between old and new locations and the complexity of conduit routing."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I move the charger outside?",
    "answer": "Yes, but outdoor installations require weatherproof-rated enclosures (NEMA 3R or 4X), weather-tight disconnect switches, and compliance with exterior conduit and grounding requirements."
  }
];
---

<Layout
  title="EV Charger Relocation in Issaquah, WA | Safe Unmount & Rewiring"
  description="Professional EV charger relocation services in Issaquah WA. Safe disconnect, rewiring, and remounting for garage remodels. Call (425) 380-0019."
  canonicalPath="/services/ev-charger-relocation/"
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Services', url: '/services/' },
    { name: 'EV Charger Relocation' }
  ]} />

  <section class="hero-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="max-width: 840px;">
        <span class="section-tag" style="background: rgba(132, 204, 22, 0.2); color: #84cc16;">Specialized EV Service</span>
        <h1>EV Charger Relocation & Remounting Service in Issaquah</h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">Remodeling your garage, converting a carport, or switching parking sides? We safely disconnect, extend wiring, and remount your charging station at its new location while maintaining full code compliance.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta-wrap">
          <a href="tel:+14253800019" class="btn btn-lime"><span>📞</span><span>Call (425) 380-0019</span></a>
          <a href="/locations/" class="btn btn-outline-white">View All 15 Service Areas</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <TrustStrip />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="rich-content" style="max-width: 900px; margin-inline: auto;">
        <h2>What This Service Covers</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Safe de-energization and disconnection of existing EVSE</li>
          <li>Extension or rerouting of 240V branch circuit conductors</li>
          <li>New conduit pathways to the updated charger mounting position</li>
          <li>Wall patching and old conduit removal at the original location</li>
          <li>Re-certification of the charging station at the new position</li>
          <li>Updated electrical permit and inspection coordination</li>
        </ul>

        <figure class="seo-service-figure" style="margin-block: 2.25rem; text-align: center;">
          <img 
            src="/images/modern-issaquah-garage-ev-charger.jpg" 
            alt="Relocating Level 2 EV charger to new garage wall position in Issaquah WA"
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            style="width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 440px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"
          />
          <figcaption style="margin-top: 0.65rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: #64748b; font-style: italic;">
            Safe unmounting, branch circuit extension, and re-mounting for garage remodels or new parking configurations.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>


        <h2>Technical Background & How It Works</h2>
        <p>Garage renovations, vehicle changes, and driveway reconfiguration are common reasons homeowners need to move their charging station. Simply unplugging a hardwired unit and moving it yourself is dangerous and violates electrical codes.</p>

        <figure class="seo-service-figure" style="margin-block: 2.25rem; text-align: center;">
          <img 
            src="/images/level-2-ev-charger-installation-issaquah.jpg" 
            alt="Surface-mounted conduit extension for relocated EV charging station in Issaquah"
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            style="width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 440px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"
          />
          <figcaption style="margin-top: 0.65rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: #64748b; font-style: italic;">
            Seamless conduit extensions protecting conductors from physical vehicle impacts and garage tools.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>


        <p>A proper relocation involves de-energizing the circuit at the breaker, disconnecting conductors, extending or rerouting wiring through new conduit, remounting the unit at the correct height and orientation, and re-terminating all connections with proper torque. If the new location increases circuit length, conductors may need upsizing to prevent voltage drop.</p>

        <p>This service is available throughout all 15 Issaquah neighborhoods, including <a href="/locations/issaquah-highlands/">Issaquah Highlands</a>, <a href="/locations/talus/">Talus</a>, <a href="/locations/klahanie/">Klahanie</a>, and <a href="/locations/olde-town-issaquah/">Olde Town Issaquah</a>. Browse our full <a href="/locations/">locations hub</a> to find your area.</p>

        <h2>When to Contact Us</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>You are remodeling your garage and the charger needs to move</li>
          <li>You changed vehicles and the charging cable no longer reaches comfortably</li>
          <li>You are converting from a wall-mounted to a pedestal-mounted setup</li>
          <li>Your parking layout changed and the charger is now on the wrong wall</li>
          <li>You are moving the charger from an interior wall to an exterior location</li>
        </ul>

        <figure class="seo-service-figure" style="margin-block: 2.25rem; text-align: center;">
          <img 
            src="/images/tesla-wall-connector-repair-installation.jpg" 
            alt="Re-certified and tested EVSE unit after garage relocation in Issaquah 98027"
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            style="width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 440px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"
          />
          <figcaption style="margin-top: 0.65rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: #64748b; font-style: italic;">
            Full post-move diagnostic testing to verify grounding continuity and full 48A charging speed.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>


        <p>For technical questions about ev charger relocation in Issaquah, call our dispatch line directly at <a href="tel:+14253800019">(425) 380-0019</a>. Licensed under <a href="https://apps.leg.wa.gov/WAC/default.aspx?cite=296-46B" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WAC 296-46B</a> and fully compliant with NEC Article 625 standards.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

